WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.190
<i>[Opening music: gentle, hopeful instrumental music fades in.]</i>

2
00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:06.360
For many young people, finishing school brings an important question:

3
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:08.340
What comes next?

4
00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.720
Finding a job can be difficult.

5
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.660
Opportunities may feel limited, and the future can seem uncertain.

6
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:22.950
This is the story of a fictional young Rwandan named Eric, who begins

7
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.730
to discover a different way of thinking about his future.

8
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.730
<i>[Sound effect: birds singing softly in the countryside.]</i>

9
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.240
Eric had been searching for work for months.

10
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.880
He wanted to become independent, support his family, and build

11
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.280
something of his own.

12
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:43.410
One day, he joined a community training session about modern

13
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.410
agriculture.

14
00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.300
At first, he was not convinced.

15
00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.130
He thought farming meant spending long days in the fields, doing

16
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.680
physically demanding work with little opportunity to grow.

17
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.850
But the training introduced him to a wider picture.

18
00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:09.300
He learned that agriculture could involve much more than planting and

19
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:09.930
harvesting.

20
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.360
Farmers and agricultural businesses also need people who understand

21
00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.080
technology,

22
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.000
marketing, transportation, food processing, and business management.

23
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.460
<i>[Music becomes slightly more uplifting.]</i>

24
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.020
Eric began exploring how digital tools could help farmers check

25
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.130
weather information,

26
00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:35.610
plan their activities, and learn about crop management.

27
00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:42.060
He also discovered opportunities beyond the farm itself, such as

28
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:43.740
packaging produce,

29
00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:48.540
connecting farmers with customers, and helping agricultural products

30
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.380
reach markets.

31
00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:57.690
With guidance from a mentor, Eric and a few friends began exploring a

32
00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:02.250
small business idea involving locally grown produce.

33
00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.780
Their plan was not guaranteed to succeed.

34
00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:12.360
They still needed training, resources, reliable customers, and money

35
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.230
to get started.

36
00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:22.050
But they now had something valuable: a clearer understanding of the

37
00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.910
possibilities available to them.

38
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.880
<i>[Brief pause.]</i>

39
00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:31.080
Eric's journey reminds us that agriculture is not simply a tradition

40
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:31.860
from the past.

41
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.230
It can also be a space for learning, innovation, and entrepreneurship.

42
00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:44.100
Technology alone cannot solve youth unemployment, and not every idea

43
00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.400
becomes a successful business.

44
00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:53.190
Access to skills, finance, markets, land, and mentorship matters.

45
00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:58.170
But when young people are given opportunities to learn and explore,

46
00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.930
new pathways may begin to emerge.

47
00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.360
<i>[Closing music rises gently.]</i>

48
00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:07.830
Sometimes, the first step toward a different future is learning to see

49
00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.680
an opportunity where you did not expect one.

50
00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:15.420
This is StoryCast: Growing Futures.

51
00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.440
<i>[Music fades out.]</i>

